liams","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/3596","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/3596"}},{"id":"3595","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"2999","description":"Ledges on the left are easiest. Center ledges have the most water and are fun. Last ledge on far right could get ugly","caption":"Ledges on left","poi_name":"Savage Falls","subject":"naterator","author":"Kevin Williams","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/3595","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/3595"}},{"id":"12478","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"8604","description":"We ran down the left side. Stay altert of the rocks and holes on the approach. Be careful of the little rock below the first drop on the left, it can knock you off line.  Avoid the sharp rock sticking out next to the big rock in the center of the second drop. Your good to go left or even center down the third drop.","caption":"Savage Falls","poi_name":"Savage Falls","subject":"","author":"Mark Cooper","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/12478","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/12478"}},{"id":"887384","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"890119","description":"View of the river right slow that crashes into a wall. Pourover at lower flows and a nasty hole with huge deflection wave off the undercut on river right. Do not run right side at higher levels. ","caption":"River right wall at high flow","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Andrew Froom","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/887384","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/887384"}},{"id":"6iDGrf5LgwMiv0rIBYPZ0","ext":"jpg","post_id":"LHAbKrrgurMZp4oEqgFHn","description":"Stay center or Left! \nSee pic! ","caption":"Strainer/Log Jam ","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Bobby Barker","poi_id":"zFJzddQE3gtSX1l9Cxtnm","photo_date":"2025-04-07T00:32:12.000Z","updated_at":"2025-04-07T00:32:12.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/6iDGrf5LgwMiv0rIBYPZ0","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/6iDGrf5LgwMiv0rIBYPZ0"}},{"id":"10182","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"7043","description":"","caption":"Little Patuxent","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"stevef","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":"2025-04-10T21:57:18.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/10182","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/10182"}},{"id":"887385","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"890120","description":"Fall line on the Little Patuxent at 1100 CFS 7.2 ft after an overnight thunderstorm. ","caption":"Fall line at 1100 CFS","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"Andrew Froom","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/887385","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/887385"}}],"detail":{"id":"730","permitUrl":null,"permitInfo":null,"description":"Park at Savage Mill and walk upstream about 1/4 mi. 'Savage Falls' consists of 3 riverwide ledges, class III+ to IV (dependent on level) with a total drop of 10-12', followed by a class III rapid that doglegs to the left. There are a few potential playspots, but it's level-dependent.\n\n[TopoZone Map](http://www.topozone.com/map.asp?z=18&n=4316876&e=352211&size=m)\n\nEd Evangelidi testifies:\n\nSavage Falls has been run successfully on river left or towards the middle with a series of basically Class 3 moves. However, each drop in this rapid has numerous pinning or boat crunching rocks. Scout carefully and be wary of rooster tails indicating hidden rocks at the bottom of any drop.","averageGradient":null,"maxGradient":null,"len